  "articleBody": "A well-planned bathroom addition starts with a site review, not fixture shopping. Confirm the location and intended use, assess nearby plumbing and electrical systems, develop a code-aware layout, establish the design and construction scope, clarify permit responsibilities, and compare written proposals. The project is ready to start when the plans, selections, pricing assumptions, and responsibilities are documented.",
